{"file":"Adapty-v2.zip","bytes":914894,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"adapty-skills","description":"Skills that hand your app's subscription surface to your agent: integrate the Adapty SDK on any mobile platform (iOS, Android, Flutter, React Native, Unity, KMP, Capacitor), run Apple Search Ads, audit a Flow Builder flow before you publish, edit a flow's config, and turn a paywall screenshot or an onboarding flow into ranked conversion tests."}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/adapty-integration/SKILL.md","name":"adapty-integration","description":"Use when a user wants to integrate Adapty SDK into a mobile app, set up in-app purchases with Adapty, add a paywall to their app, or move to Adapty from another purchase system. Triggers on \"integrate Adapty\", \"add Adapty to my app\", \"set up subscriptions\", \"add a paywall\", \"migrate from RevenueCat\", \"replace RevenueCat with Adapty\", \"move off Superwall\", or similar.","headings":["Adapty SDK Integration","Overview","State Tracking","Phase 0: Setup","Fetching Adapty docs","Session marker","Feedback consent","Phase 1: Analyze the project","Phase 2: Ask three questions","Phase 3: Dashboard setup","Step 1: Authenticate","Step 2: Get or create the app","Step 3: Get the access level ID","both --sdk-id and --title are required","Step 3.5: Check existing dashboard config (existing apps only)","Step 4: Create products","--period options: weekly, monthly, two_months, trimonthly, semiannual, annual, lifetime","--title is the Adapty dashboard label (internal); not visible to end users"],"name_hint":"adapty · 集成","description_zh":"将 Adapty SDK 接入移动应用，配置应用内购买、订阅和付费墙，或从 RevenueCat、Superwall 等购买系统迁移到 Adapty。"},{"path":"skills/ads-manager/SKILL.md","name":"ads-manager","description":"Use when managing Apple Search Ads through the Adapty CLI — reading campaign, ad group, keyword or ad performance, changing bids or budgets, adding or pausing keywords, launching or pausing a campaign, creating a whole campaign structure in bulk from JSON or an Apple Ads template, harvesting search terms, or setting up rule-based ad automations.","headings":["Apple Search Ads through the Adapty CLI","The CLI","Account surface","The two templates","One question, one call","Never","Rationalizations","Red Flags — STOP","Workflows","Anything not covered here"],"name_hint":"ads · manager","description_zh":"通过 Adapty CLI 管理 Apple Search Ads，查看活动、广告组、关键词和广告表现，调整出价预算、启停关键词/活动，按 JSON 或模板批量建结构、挖掘搜索词并配置规则自动化。"},{"path":"skills/flow-audit/SKILL.md","name":"flow-audit","description":"Use when a client asks whether a Flow Builder flow is ready for production, wants it audited or checked, or asks something like \"did I forget anything — triggers, products, variables?\", \"is this ready to publish?\", or \"check my paywall/flow\". Answers one question — is this flow safe to put in front of paying users — with a verdict and ranked findings. Read-only: never writes to a flow. Complements `flow-generator` (which owns writes) and `paywall-teardown` (which owns conversion advice).","headings":["flow-audit","What this answers","Phase 1 — resolve and authenticate","Phase 2 — select the flow","Phase 3 — fetch","Phase 4 — check","Phase 5 — report","The verdict rule","What you cannot check","Handoff","Reference","Boundaries"],"name_hint":"流量 · 审查","description_zh":"只读审查 Adapty Flow Builder 流程是否适合向付费用户上线，检查触发器、商品、变量等遗漏并输出结论与按重要性排序的问题；修改流程和转化建议分别由 flow-generator、paywall-teardown 负责。"},{"path":"skills/flow-generator/SKILL.md","name":"flow-generator","description":"Use when a user wants to change an Adapty flow by editing its builder config JSON — add a locale, translate a paywall or onboarding, rewrite copy, add/remove/reorder screens, add tabs or plan pickers, wire quiz branching, or build an onboarding sequence. Triggers on \"edit my flow config\", \"add a language to my paywall\", \"translate my onboarding\", \"remove a screen from the flow\", \"add tabs to my paywall\", \"build me a paywall like this\", \"build me an onboarding\", or a supplied Adapty flow config.","headings":["Flow generator","What you print","The CLI surface","The five phases","1. Resolve the invocation, then authenticate","2. New flow, or existing flow","3. Check the shape, then clear the publish gate","4. Preview, and iterate until it looks right","5. Get approval, then deliver — a write or a file","one call: re-read the lock and write under it, because your own last write invalidated it","The link alone — the default. No image, no window, no `qrcode` dependency.","Add a QR as well, when it will actually be scanned:","… --qr --md-base <your working directory>","Safety","Verify","References"],"name_hint":"流量 · generator","description_zh":"编辑 Adapty Flow Builder 配置 JSON，支持新增语言、翻译付费墙/引导、改写文案、增删排序屏幕、添加标签页或方案选择器、配置问答分支和生成引导序列。"},{"path":"skills/onboarding-teardown/SKILL.md","name":"onboarding-teardown","description":"Use when someone wants to improve, fix, test or critique a mobile app's onboarding — \"here's my onboarding\", \"roast my flow\", \"why do users drop off before the paywall\", a competitor's signup flow, a welcome or activation flow, a quiz, or a flow described in one sentence. Also use whenever YOU are the one designing or generating an onboarding sequence and were given no design reference to follow — no reference screens, no existing flow to copy, no spelled-out sequence — as in \"build me an onboarding\", \"add a quiz before the paywall\", \"make a flow that converts\"; this library is the reference in that case, and it evaluates and corrects the flow you produce. Also use when reviewing an onboarding flow config or a set of `flows config preview` renders produced by the flow-generator skill. Do not wait to be asked for a \"teardown\" by name.","headings":["Onboarding Teardown","Input","When you have the config, read it — don't interview","The six questions — ask ONE AT A TIME","Interview rules","Optional screens","Reference","Two directions","Choose the flow skeleton first","Process (internal — do NOT show these steps in the output)","Output — audit","Output — design","What you cannot invent","The disclaimer, verbatim","The CTA","Rules","Scope"],"name_hint":"入门/入职 · teardown","description_zh":"评审和改善移动应用引导、欢迎、激活或问答流程，分析付费墙前流失；也为缺少设计参考的新引导提供参考并检查生成结果，支持 flow-generator 配置和预览审查。"},{"path":"skills/paywall-teardown/SKILL.md","name":"paywall-teardown","description":"Use when someone shares a mobile subscription or purchase screen and wants to know what to change, fix, test or improve — \"here's my paywall\", \"roast this\", \"what should I test\", a competitor screenshot, a design in progress, or an image with almost no text. Also use whenever YOU are the one designing or generating a paywall screen and were given no design reference to follow — no reference image, no existing screen to copy, no layout spec — as in \"make me a paywall\", \"make one that converts\", \"will this convert?\", \"is this any good?\"; this library is the reference in that case, and it evaluates and corrects the screen you produce. Also use when reviewing a paywall render or flow config produced by the flow-generator skill. Do not wait to be asked for a \"teardown\" by name.","headings":["Paywall Teardown","Input","Reference","Two directions","Choose the archetype first","Process (internal — do NOT show these steps in the output)","Output — audit","Output — design","What you cannot invent","The disclaimer, verbatim","The CTA","Framing rules (these protect credibility — a sharp growth lead will poke)","Scope note"],"name_hint":"paywall · teardown","description_zh":"评审移动订阅或购买屏幕，结合现有页面、竞品截图或草案提出修改和测试建议；也为缺少设计参考的新付费墙提供参考并校正生成页面，支持 flow-generator 结果审查。"}],"commands":[],"readmes":[{"path":"README.md","headings":["Adapty Skills","The toolkit","Install","Claude Code","Any agentic CLI","Copy the directories","or manually:","Integrating the SDK","Flow & paywall approaches","Managing Apple Search Ads","Auditing a flow","Building flows and paywalls","Tearing down a paywall","Tearing down an onboarding flow","Requirements","Corporate environments with a domain allowlist","Feedback"]},{"path":"tests/README.md","headings":["tests/","The corpus","The tools","Which tool catches what","`render-measure.py` — measure a render instead of eyeballing it","`test-audit-flow.py` — the calibration suite for `flow-audit`","`test-id-hygiene.py` — the black-screen class, and the scope that is the finding","`test-flowkit.py` — the guardrail on the authoring helpers","`test-snippet.py` — the guardrail on save/reuse","`schema-check.py` — validating against the published schema"]},{"path":"feedback-endpoint/README.md","headings":["Adapty SDK Integration — Feedback Endpoint","Deploy","Endpoint","Validation","Tests"]}],"mcp_servers":[],"config_names":[],"paths":[".claude-plugin/marketplace.json",".claude-plugin/plugin.json",".github/workflows/skill-lints.yml",".gitignore","CLAUDE.md","README.md","context7.json","docs/green-round-gate.md","feedback-endpoint/.gitignore","feedback-endpoint/README.md","feedback-endpoint/api/sdk-integration-feedback.js","feedback-endpoint/package.json","feedback-endpoint/src/validate.js","feedback-endpoint/test/endpoint.test.js","scripts/app-side-allowlist.txt","scripts/lint-links.mjs","scripts/lint-symbols.mjs","scripts/shared.mjs","scripts/undocumented-sdk-symbols.txt","skills/adapty-integration/SKILL.md","skills/adapty-integration/references/android.md","skills/adapty-integration/references/capacitor.md","skills/adapty-integration/references/flutter.md","skills/adapty-integration/references/ios.md","skills/adapty-integration/references/kmp.md","skills/adapty-integration/references/migration-architecture.md","skills/adapty-integration/references/migration-flow-rebuild.md","skills/adapty-integration/references/migration-revenuecat-activation.md","skills/adapty-integration/references/migration-revenuecat-attribution.md","skills/adapty-integration/references/migration-revenuecat-entitlements.md","skills/adapty-integration/references/migr